PRE-TABLE BLOCK -- #524 armbdt, TABLE 4 (the CLASS CLOSURE)
===========================================================
SEPARATE FILE, not an append.  A PRETABLE's mtime is its whole evidentiary
value and this ledger records an append destroying one once.

WHY A FOURTH TABLE.  Table 3 closed M_MASK1 (27/29).  The repair-chain pass
then found TWO MORE clean-sweep candidates against the 29-row composite --
both static deductions, not measured, which is why they are legs here:

  M_MASK7     `& ~7' -- OVER-alignment.  Every base the instrument drove
              (0x10000, 0x2000{1,2}, 0x2100{1,2}) sits in the FIRST word of
              its 8-byte block, where ~3 and ~7 AGREE.  Swept all 29.

  M_PBITCOND  a CONDITIONAL weakening on an EXISTING dominating predicate:
              mask ~1 when p_bit, ~3 otherwise, at the STORE site only.
              ARM STM is IA (p_bit=0, correct mask); Thumb PUSH is DB
              (p_bit=1, weakened) but ran at exactly ONE residue, +1, where
              ~1 and ~3 AGREE.  Swept all 29.

TWO CONSECUTIVE PASSES FOUND MASK-WEAKENING BREACHES, SO THIS IS A CLASS
CLOSURE, NOT A THIRD POINT FIX.  The rule: enumerate the full space from the
function's own inputs and close every cell in ONE diff.

THE SPACE, from the helpers' own inputs:
    {site: load, store} x {residue: 0,1,2,3} x {word position in the 8-byte
    block} x {p_bit: pre-index, post-index}

Previously exercised: residue {0,1} at word 0 with p_bit=0 (plus p_bit=1 at
residue 1 only).  THE UNCOVERED CELLS WERE: residue 2 (closed in table 3),
word position 1, and p_bit=1 at any residue where ~1 and ~3 differ.

ROWS ADDED THIS PASS -- three cells, ONE diff:
  ARM_LDM_COLD_DATA_BIT2   base 0x20005.  ~3 -> 0x20004 -> 0x55667788.
                           ~7 -> 0x20000 -> 0x11223344.  KILLS M_MASK7 (load).
  ARM_STM_COLD_DATA_BIT2   base 0x21005.  ~3 puts the word at PAGE_STM+4;
                           ~7 puts it at PAGE_STM.  BOTH halves asserted, so
                           it cannot pass on absence alone.  KILLS M_MASK7
                           (store).
  THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2  sp 0x23006, stmdb -> 0x23002.  ~3 -> 0x23000 ->
                           0x11223344.  ~1 -> 0x23002, straddling ->
                           0x33440000.  KILLS M_PBITCOND.

DISCLOSED, NOT ROWED
--------------------
  *** THE PATH ROWS ARE FIXTURE CHECKS, NOT MUTATION DISCRIMINATORS, AND THE
  REPAIR PASS WAS RIGHT ABOUT MY OWN NEW ONES. ***  Every in_tlb_* value is
  captured BEFORE run_prog, so no helper-local mutation of a mask, operand or
  predicate can retroactively change it.  They establish that the run really
  was cold -- which the core comparison needs -- and they discriminate NO
  enumerated mutant.  Kept for that purpose and disclosed as such rather than
  counted toward the floor.

  RESIDUE 3: "a +3 row buys no enumerated mutant" was TOO BROAD as a claim
  about the COMPOSITE.  It holds within a fixed cell -- if B+1 and B+2 both
  map correctly to B, the mask clears both low bits, so B+3 does too.  What it
  missed is the PREDICATE/RESIDUE COMBINATION: a Thumb PUSH +3 would kill
  M_PBITCOND, and so would a Thumb PUSH +2.  The +2 form is rowed above;
  residue 3 remains unrowed and is disclosed as one possible witness among
  several, not as buying nothing.

PREDICTIONS -- PREDICTIONS ONLY.  Measured values go to SCORES.txt and every
citation names that file.
  BASE        clean
  M_MASK1     RED on the two P2 rows
  M_MASK7     MUST GO RED on the two BIT2 rows
  M_PBITCOND  MUST GO RED on THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2
  If either new mutant survives, the closure has failed and #524 does not ship.
